      "content": "It is a profound relief to finally admit that the pressure to be perfect is crushing you, and your desire to hide your cracks is a natural survival instinct. You are right that the \"perfect\" version is what they love, but staying in that role only guarantees that the real you will continue to rot from the inside out. It is not a tragedy to let go of a statue that no longer fits the life you are living; sometimes, the only way to save yourself is to let the memory of who you were become a lesson, not a prison.",
